    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40918" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕgressĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		regredior, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a going back</i>, <i>return; a
				retiring</i>, <i>retreat</i> (postAug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maturata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 122, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vespertina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 9</span></i>
			, p. 227, 17: non incruenta, Front. Princ. Hist. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, a fig. of rhetoric, <i>repetition</i>, the Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπάνοδος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				3, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Rufin. Schem. Lex.
			19</span></i> (p. 252 Frotsch.).</div>
